  "candidates": [
    {
      "id": "REVIEW-BELFRY-SHELL-ZERO-EDGE-001",
      "severity": "P3 provisional; a zero horizontal belfry-stage edge causes invalid normalization if an externally altered or decoded plan reaches the public shell compiler",
      "classification": "current source trace of the same conditional positive-footprint contract in recovered checkpoint 059; no unique historical finding inferred",
      "detail": "SmallChurchPlan is public and derived Serde, its belfry_stage is a general SpatialBounds whose checked construction and deserialization permit equal endpoints, and BuildingPlan retains that field. compile_building_lod documents an accepted semantic plan, dispatches a present small church to the shell compiler, and append_belfry normalizes all four stage edges without a positive-horizontal-extent check. A stage with min.x == max.x, finite z and positive other spans has a zero first and third edge. The locked glam source implements normalize as vector times reciprocal length and conditionally asserts its finite result; for an exact zero edge the IEEE arithmetic is non-finite when assertion is disabled, and the assertion can panic when its relevant feature configuration is active. Feature resolution and execution were not checked.",
      "consumer_and_safeguards": "If non-finite normalization returns, append_belfry passes it as the InteriorTimber quad normal and into UV projection. LodMesh::push_quad retains those supplied attributes, and remap_vertices preserves vertices for a non-finite tangent determinant rather than repairing their inputs. A selected tactical render adapter copies position, normal and UV attributes and requests tangent generation, but the actual downstream handling, error or displayed effect is not established. The ordinary Fittings::assemble producer sets x and z to centre \u00b11.05 m, producing a positive 2.1 m footprint in its fixed programme. The public compiler calls its input an accepted plan; no supported decoded or manually changed plan, full audit outcome, renderer run or gameplay incident has been shown. The specifically inspected small-church audit checks authority and public-aisle overlap, not belfry_stage; other validators and callers remain open.",
      "connected_scope": "SmallChurchPlan accepted-plan admission and positive footprint ownership; generator and public plan ingress; shell edge normalization; LodMesh writer and remapping; tactical recipe mesh and tangent generation; whole-plan validation and historical aliases.",
      "proposed_repair": "After completing the audit and receiving implementation authorization, decide whether non-generated plans are supported and establish positive horizontal extents at the purpose-owned small-church or accepted-plan boundary, or explicitly reject invalid input before normalization. Preserve valid zero extents in general SpatialBounds and do not add compatibility shims.",
      "later_acceptance": "When product validation is authorized, cover supported positive stages for all chapel/parish sizes, zero and near-zero stage edges according to the decided contract, finite mesh attributes, and error propagation through supported plan and render paths.",
      "historical_related_candidates": [
        "PL13-050-BELFRY-POSITIVE-FOOTPRINT"
      ],
      "relationship_qualification": "The recovered 059 contract already identifies this same conditional first failure and positive generator safeguard, and remains at its original revision with no accepted unique finding. This current trace adds selected native, remap and adapter evidence but does not close global aliases, reconcile the historical queue or restore checkpoint 3821.",
      "discovery": "partial; supported accepted-plan ingress, feature resolution, all validators and consumers, rendering, aliases and independent lenses remain open",
      "repair": "not started",
      "validation": "not performed"
    }
